  "body": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\" data-mode=\"public\" data-zone=\"topics\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\" />\n<title>Canadian polling industry — signed analysis — CANOPTICON</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"The Canadian polling industry operates with relatively weak oversight and a dominant market player.\" />\n\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\" />\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" crossorigin />\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500;600&family=Newsreader:ital,opsz,wght@0,6..72,400;0,6..72,500;0,6..72,600;1,6..72,400;1,6..72,500;1,6..72,600&display=swap\" />\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/styles.css?v=bos3ko\" />\n<link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/svg+xml\" href=\"/favicon.svg\" />\n<link rel=\"alternate icon\" href=\"/favicon.ico\" />\n</head>\n<body>\n<nav class=\"nav\">\n  <div class=\"nav-inner\">\n    <a href=\"/\" class=\"wordmark\">CANOPTICON<span class=\"dot\">·</span><span class=\"wordmark-sub\">The standing record</span></a>\n    <input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"nav-toggle\" class=\"nav-toggle\" />\n    <label for=\"nav-toggle\" class=\"nav-burger\" aria-label=\"Menu\"><span></span></label>\n    <div class=\"nav-links\">\n      <a href=\"/\">Record</a>\n      <a href=\"/investigations\">Investigations</a>\n      <a href=\"/watchlist\">Watchlist</a>\n      <a href=\"/method\">Method</a>\n      <a href=\"/search\" class=\"nav-search\"><span class=\"q\">/</span> ask the record</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</nav>\n<main class=\"record-main\">\n<div class=\"container\">\n<article class=\"subject-page subject-page-signed\">\n  <div class=\"reveal-tabs\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Facts or analysis\">\n  <a class=\"reveal-tab\" href=\"/p/canadian-polling-industry\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"false\">Facts</a>\n  <a class=\"reveal-tab on\" href=\"/p/canadian-polling-industry?mode=signed\" role=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Analysis</a>\n</div>\n\n  \n  \n  <header class=\"signed-head\">\n    <div class=\"kicker\"><span class=\"intent-badge intent-assessment\">Assessment</span> <span class=\"kicker-meta\">Analysis · Signed</span></div>\n    <h1>Canadian polling industry</h1>\n    <blockquote class=\"thesis-block\">\"The Canadian polling industry operates with relatively weak oversight and a dominant market player.\"</blockquote>\n    <div class=\"signature-block\">\n      <div class=\"signature\">— signed</div>\n      <div class=\"signature-meta\">22 July 2026 · moderate confidence · 4 claims verified</div>\n    </div>\n  </header>\n  <div class=\"prose signed-body\"><p>The Canadian polling industry stands out for its weaker disclosure rules compared to the UK's British Polling Council (BPC) [q1]. Unlike the US, which has the American Association of Public Opinion Research (AAPOR) with robust enforcement mechanisms, Canada lacks an independent regulator with similar teeth [q2]. This regulatory environment coexists with a market dominated by a single aggregator, 338Canada [q3].</p>\n<p>According to some critics, these factors have contributed to a concerning state of affairs, with the industry purportedly being 'hollowed out into a federally subsidized, methodologically opaque, AI-experimentation playground' [q4].</p>\n<p>While this critical view suggests that the industry's issues run deep, it is essential to consider that the presence of a dominant aggregator and weaker rules could also simply facilitate a more streamlined, albeit less transparent, polling environment. The critical assertion that the industry has been fundamentally compromised remains a viewpoint, not a verified fact.</p>\n<p>The actual impact of these factors on the industry's overall integrity and effectiveness remains a topic for further investigation.</p></div>\n  \n  <section id=\"claims\" class=\"signed-claims\">\n  <div class=\"sec-k\">Claims &amp; receipts</div>\n  <div class=\"fact\" id=\"claim-2e636c36-7503-4a19-9fd0-774a3f23422e\">\n  <div class=\"fact-line\"><p class=\"fact-text\">a single dominant aggregator (338Canada)</p></div>\n  \n  <details class=\"rcpt\">\n  <summary><span class=\"rdoc\">PASS 4 — The Researchers, The Natural Experiments, and the T</span></summary>\n  <div class=\"rcpt-body\">\n    <div class=\"rcpt-q\">“a single dominant aggregator (338Canada)”</div>\n    <div class=\"rcpt-src\"><span>SOURCE</span><a href=\"/library/compass-artifact-wf-b84cf8d0-c9fe-46d0-bdad-b6853f4544ef-text-markdown\">PASS 4 — The Researchers, The Natural Experiments, and the T</a><span class=\"sep\">·</span><span>stored copy on file</span></div>\n    <div class=\"rcpt-v\">VERIFIED — a word-for-word match in the stored source</div>\n  </div>\n</details>\n</div><div class=\"fact\" id=\"claim-c5ae08c9-99c9-4b31-9c89-9bb6c2139315\">\n  <div class=\"fact-line\"><p class=\"fact-text\">the Canadian polling industry has been hollowed out into a federally subsidized, methodologically opaque, AI-experimentation playground</p></div>\n  <p class=\"fact-text\" style=\"margin-top:2px\"><i>Claimed by UNKNOWN</i></p>\n  <details class=\"rcpt\">\n  <summary><span class=\"rdoc\">PASS 4 — The Researchers, The Natural Experiments, and the T</span></summary>\n  <div class=\"rcpt-body\">\n    <div class=\"rcpt-q\">“the Canadian polling industry has been hollowed out into a federally subsidized, methodologically opaque, AI-experimentation playground”</div>\n    <div class=\"rcpt-src\"><span>SOURCE</span><a href=\"/library/compass-artifact-wf-b84cf8d0-c9fe-46d0-bdad-b6853f4544ef-text-markdown\">PASS 4 — The Researchers, The Natural Experiments, and the T</a><span class=\"sep\">·</span><span>stored copy on file</span></div>\n    <div class=\"rcpt-v\">VERIFIED — a word-for-word match in the stored source</div>\n  </div>\n</details>\n</div>\n</section>\n  <section class=\"face